1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,128
This founder was so desperate, she had a professor invent 4 million customers.

2
00:00:04,328 --> 00:00:08,118
And JPMorgan bought it. For $175 million.

3
00:00:08,568 --> 00:00:11,684
Her startup, Frank, claimed 4.25 million users.

4
00:00:11,984 --> 00:00:14,742
Hit like if you've ever padded a number. Just not like this.

5
00:00:15,042 --> 00:00:18,463
The SEC says the real number was fewer than 300,000.

6
00:00:18,863 --> 00:00:24,329
So when JPMorgan asked to see the customer list, how do you hand over 4 million people who don't exist?

7
00:00:24,679 --> 00:00:29,405
According to the SEC, she first asked her own engineer to make fake data. He said no.

8
00:00:29,755 --> 00:00:35,077
So prosecutors say a data science professor built a list of over 4 million fake customers instead.

9
00:00:35,427 --> 00:00:38,467
Send this to the friend who always rounds up their follower count.

10
00:00:38,767 --> 00:00:44,108
The bank paid $175 million. That's about $580 for every real user.

11
00:00:44,458 --> 00:00:46,885
Follow along, because the ending is the best part.

12
00:00:47,185 --> 00:00:50,373
Guilty on all 4 counts. 85 months in prison.

13
00:00:50,773 --> 00:00:53,794
Restitution: $287.5 million.

14
00:00:54,194 --> 00:00:57,587
4 million customers. Fewer than 300,000 were real.

